    <rule id="469df92c-cf8a-7217-5827-4b5308be4d1f-d4a5a" name="Jam!" page="" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
      <description>If the number of shots fired is a double 1's, the weapon is treated as though it had been affect by a Weapon Destroyed result, but loses no Hull Points.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="b4c50a82-b04f-ea02-f573-c8b2867c8daa-d4a5a" name="Jury-rigged Lifta-droppa" page="116" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
      <description>Select an enemy vehicle wich began the game with no more than 4 Hull Points and roll to Hit.  If the target is hit, roll a D6.

1 - Roll on the Jury rigged Lifta-droppa Mishaps table below.  (Note from GW:  Yes, you just rolled on a table to get to roll on a different table.  Suck it Ork Player!!!)

2-5  -  The target vehicle is thrown D" in a random dirrection (roll a scatter), stopping if it moves to within 1" from any other model, and takes D3 Glancing hits.

6  -  The target vehicle is thrown 2D6" in a random direction (roll a scatter), stopping if it moves to within 1" away from any other model, and suffers an Explodes! result on the Vehicle Damage table.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="7436e461-4f08-b7fe-07d3-a2b6f67aa7f5-d4a5a" name="Kaptin Badrukk's Flash Gitz" page="62" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
      <description>During deployment, the controlling player can choose to form Kaptin Badrukk and all of the units of Flash Gitz in this Formation into a single unit known as Kaptin Badrukk's Flash Gitz.  Badrukk cannot leave this unit.  Kaptin Badrukk's Flash Gitz counts as 3 units for Victory Points purposes if it is completely destroyed.</description>
    </rule>
