      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
      <description>1 Supa-shootist
2 Waaagh!-mongerer
3 Madboy
4 A Kunnin' Plan
5 Kallin' in a Favour
6 Dead 'Ard</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="dee47bd5-da9f-f4df-4eac-26b6ae43e8e1-d4a5a" name="Warphead" page="0" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
    </rule>
    <rule id="e26065d4-edff-b29a-4a4d-4032a722fed6-d4a5a" name="What Grukk Says Goes" page="29" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
    </rule>
    <rule id="5ef5e4f3-bbd5-6fa9-a301-b9d6c88cd813-d4a5a" name="Whirrr Click-click" page="96" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
      <description>If a double is rolled when determining the number of shots for any of the supa-gatler's shooting attacks, then it runs out of ammunition after that attack has been resolved and cannot shoot again for the rest of the battle. Tis does not apply to the very first shooting attack a supa-gatler makes in battle (so it will fire a minimum of two times before running out of ammunition).</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="209ba0ab-7282-650b-a990-398e59fc2570-d4a5a" name="Wild Rampage" page="118" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
    </rule>
    <rule id="099b219f-0a6f-9ae1-4e23-b1ae0bb04270-d4a5a" name="Zzap" page="0" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
      <description>Each time a Zzap gun is fired, roll 2D6 to determine its Strength, after the target unit has been chosen.  If the roll is above 10, the shot is resolved at Strenght 10 and the weapon Gets Hot on any To Hit roll of 1, 2, or 3.  If a Zzap gun Gets Hot, the Wound is resolved against the crew. Zzap guns automatically cause a Crew Shaken result in addition to any other effects when they score a glancing or penetrating hit.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="8f31-befe-f557-4a58-d4a5a" name="Prophet of Gork and Mork" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
      <description>If Ghazghkull is your Warlord, he gains a 2+ Invul save on any turn he calls a Waaagh! This invulnerable save lasts until the start of his next turn. In addition, Ghazghkull and all other models in his unit that are equipped with mega armour can Run on a turn he calls a Waaagh! despite having the Slow and Purposeful special rule (which is conferred by wearing mega armour).</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="db4b-9236-0c83-3222-d4a5a" name="Warlord Trait 3: Like a Thunderbolt!" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
      <description>The Warlord, and all friendly units with the Orks Faction within 12" of him, can re-roll all the dice when determining Run moves or charge ranges.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="9d9b-f159-c971-a10c-d4a5a" name="Warlord Trait 6: Might is Right" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
      <description>The Warlord receives +1 to the Strength characteristic on his profile.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="9a07-3671-2106-3665-d4a5a" name="Irrational Genius (Warlord Trait)" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
      <description>An army that includes a Warlord with this ability must select one friendly vehicle chosen from the Ork Dread Mob army list after it has been deployed, and roll on the table below, applying the result to the vehicle. This effect may not be used on Super-heavy vehicles, or vehicles that form part of a squadron. 

1-2 - Scrap Covered Monstrosity: If this vehicle had the fast type, it loses it. If it did not have the fast type, it becomes Heavy.  In addition it gains +1 Hull Point

3-4 -Supa Turbo-thrusta:  If the vehicle has the Heavy type it loses it, and if it did not have the Heavy type it gains the jink special rule.  On any turn in which the vehicle does not move Flat Out, it may choose to activate the Supa Turbo-thrusta in the Shooting phase.  When it does so roll a D6.  On a 1, the vehicle is Immobilized but doesn't lose a hull point for the next turn.  This does not cause a flyer to crash.  On a 2-6 The vehicle immediately moves 2D6* directly fowards.  If it contacts any enemy vehicles or units, it is considered to have either Rammed or Tank Shocked them as appropiate and ends its movement after resolving the attack.

During a Supa Turbo-thrusta move the vehicle is unaffected by difficult terrain, but takes dangerous terrain tests as normal.  Stop if the move would take you into impassible terrain.

5-6 -  Armour Burnin' Dakka: The controlling player may, in any turn or phase, choose to fire any of the weapons on the vehicle using the Armour Burnin' Dakka when they would normally be allowed to shoot with the vehicle - this choice is made before any dice are rolled for that shot.  The chosen Weapons gain the Rending and Gets Hot special rules.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="bd04-bf9e-0215-261f-d4a5a" name="Mega Charga" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
      <description>Once per game at the star of any Movement phase roll a D6.  On a 1, the Meka-dread is immobilised, but the vehicle doesn't lose a hull point. 2-6, the Meka-dread gains fleet.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="e28c-17a1-822f-c8dc-d4a5a" name="Metal Monstas" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
      <description>If no other HQ choices are included in an Ork Dread Mob army then a Meka-dread must be the army's Warlord, and gains the following trait:

At the beginning of any of its own turns, the Meka-dread may choose to join any friendly Deff Dread Mob as long as it is within 4".   The Meka-dread then couts as part of that vehicle squadron.  It may choose to leave the squad at the start of any of it's subsequent turns. </description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="113e-f501-2b5e-e946-d4a5a" name="Fixin' Klaws" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
      <description>A Meka-dread counts as having a set of Mek's tools, and may attempt to fix itself or other vehicles when not affect by a Crew Stunned or Crew Shaken result.

In addition, the Meka Dread gains Rage.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="e140-1fee-66ef-a8a6-d4a5a" name="The Dok is in!" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
      <description>For each Pain Boss included in the army, the controlling player may select a single friendly Spanna Boyz unit.  The selected unit may be upgrade to have Cybork bodies for +3 Points per model.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="0e0f-1d72-6296-4dc5-d4a5a" name="Mad Doc" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
      <description>If a Pain Boss is selected as your army's warlord then he recieves the following trait:

An army that includes a Painboss as its Warlord may include a single unit of Cybork Slashas as a Troops choice.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="e6a2-af47-21dd-9d75-d4a5a" name="Dok's 'Speriments" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
      <description>At the start of the game, before deployment, roll once for each unit of Cybork Slashas.

1-2  -  Turbo-killas: The unit gains Fleet, Move Through Cover, and Hammer of Wrath, but every time it Runs or Charges it must roll a D6 for each member of the mob.  On a 1, the mob takes a single wound (armor saves may be taken)

3-4  -  Tinboy Brutes: The unit increasees its Toughness by +1 and gains Slow and Purposeful

5-6  -  Short Circuit: Select either of the other 2 results, however, at the start of each of the controlling player's turns roll a D6 for this mob.  On a 1, the unit may not move, fire or charge in that turn.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="30cd-0d70-bdbd-f6b4-d4a5a" name="Boom Kannisters" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
      <description>Boom Kannisters are fired in a straight line away from a point on the vehicle's side, and their target point for scatter is always their maximum listed range.</description>
    </rule>
    <rule id="d76c-49fe-c8f8-54ef-d4a5a" name="Lifta Droppa Mishaps table" hidden="false">
      <profiles />
      <rules />
      <infoLinks />
      <modifiers />
      <description>1 - Boom!: The lifta Wagon suffers an Explodes result.
2 -  Aaaagh, it's glowin'!:  The lifta Wagon suffers a penetrating hit, and all models within d6" of the vehicle suffer a S2 AP3 hit.
3-4 - Fizzzz!: The Lifta Wagon suffers a Glancing hit.
5 - Flyin'!: Resolve the effects of a Lifta-droppa on the Lifta Wagon itself.
6 - Out'a control!: The opposing player picks a new target for the Lifta=droppa's attack within range and Line of Sigh, and the attack is resolved again.  Further rolls of 1 are a failed shot.</description>
    </rule>
